  "worked_solution": "The existential quantifier \"$\u2203$\" means \"there exists.\" So, the statement \n$\u2203m\\in N,\\,I(m)$ \nreads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $m\\in N$ **such that** ${3}^{m}$ is prime.\n\n**Note:** This statement is true because ${3}^{1}=3$ is a prime number.",
